 A small TypeScript library, with no runtime dependency, of building blocks for our services that store,
 exchange and update JSON: configuration files, API payloads and stored records. It is imported by the
 other projects of the team, so its behaviour must follow the published standards it implements.
+
+## JSON Pointer
+
+`resolvePointer(document, pointer)` returns the value a JSON Pointer (RFC 6901) refers to in a JSON
+document. It throws when the pointer is malformed (not empty and not starting with `/`, or a `~` not
+followed by `0` or `1`) or when it does not resolve to a value of the document.
+
+```ts
+import { resolvePointer } from 'json-toolkit';
+
+resolvePointer({ a: { 'b/c': [10, 20] } }, '/a/b~1c/1'); // 20
+resolvePointer({ a: 1 }, '/b'); // throws
+```
